class:: DeJongMap
summary:: Trigger-driven raw Peter de Jong map coordinates
categories:: UGens>Generators>Chaotic>Maps
related:: Guides/Stochastica, Classes/CliffordMap

description::

Peter de Jong maps operate similarly to Clifford attractors, using a system of sine and cosine functions. However, their specific coupling creates tightly folded, continuous curves that rapidly swoop and wrap around themselves. Conceptually, this generates LFO-like signals that are extremely sensitive to initial parameters. A slight change in parameters entirely morphs the shape of the modulation, allowing for highly interactive, fluid, and chaotic performance control signals.

Implements Peter de Jong's recurrence code::x' = sin(a*y) - cos(b*x):: and code::y' = sin(c*x) - cos(d*y)::. The exact equation is stated because related attractor formulas have several naming conventions.

The outputs are raw state coordinates. They are not normalized audio signals and may diverge for some parameters.

Like link::Classes/Stepper::, DeJongMap advances on trigger edges; unlike Stepper, it computes two coupled trigonometric coordinates.

subsection:: State-space portrait

image::dejong-map-phase.png#The Peter de Jong attractor at the documented defaults. x is horizontal and y is vertical; density, rather than a connected line, describes this discrete orbit.::

classmethods::

method:: ar
argument:: trig
Advance on a rising edge.
argument:: a
Sine coefficient in the x equation.
argument:: b
Cosine coefficient in the x equation.
argument:: c
Sine coefficient in the y equation.
argument:: d
Cosine coefficient in the y equation.
argument:: x0
Initial x coordinate.
argument:: y0
Initial y coordinate.
argument:: reset
Restore initial coordinates on a rising edge.
returns:: Two audio-rate outputs: x and y.

method:: kr
Control-rate version with the same arguments and outputs.

instancemethods::

examples::

code::
(
{ DeJongMap.ar(Impulse.ar(900))[1] * 0.08 }.play
)
::

code::
(
{ Pan2.ar(Decay2.ar(Impulse.ar(12), 0.001, 0.04), DeJongMap.kr(Impulse.kr(12))[0].tanh) * 0.1 }.play
)
::

code::
// Chaotic Flanger Modulation
(
{
    var trig, coords, source, delay;
    trig = Impulse.kr(30);
    coords = DeJongMap.kr(trig);
    source = Saw.ar([150, 151]) * 0.1;
    // Folded trigonometric swoops mapped to extremely sensitive delay times
    delay = coords[0].linlin(-2, 2, 0.001, 0.02);
    CombL.ar(source, 0.1, delay, 0.5)
}.play;
)
::




subsection:: Real-time phase portrait

code::
(
SDPhaseView.open(
    "Peter de Jong map: x-y phase portrait",
    [-2.1, 2.1], [-2.1, 2.1],
    { DeJongMap.kr(Impulse.kr(120)) },
    { |state|
        Pan2.ar(
            SinOsc.ar(state[0].clip(-2.1, 2.1).linexp(-2.1, 2.1, 100, 1800), 0, 0.06),
            state[1].clip(-2.1, 2.1).linlin(-2.1, 2.1, -1, 1)
        )
    }
);
)
::
